    "data": {
      "A": "Research the serial algorithmic replacement: use a stable O(rows log rows) comparison sort with reusable scratch, then replace quadratic mode counting with a linear equal-run scan. Return -1 when nothing repeats; retain the first sorted value on frequency ties and the source's float conversion of the selected mode. Preserve signed-zero ordering and provide a correctness-preserving fallback for exceptional floating-point cases where ordinary sorting/run counting is not equivalent. Eliminate uninitialized counting rather than depending on allocator contents; report any resulting oracle incompatibility without altering validation. Keep arithmetic and harmonic accumulation in input order and variance accumulation in sorted order. Measure the complete program, since replacing only sorting leaves quadratic mode work.",
      "B": "Research input/output overhead independently. Compare fscanf with buffered input and correctly rounded conversion such as strtod, preserving accepted numeric syntax, whitespace, token boundaries, EOF handling, and unrestricted double values. Retain the existing column-major compute layout initially. Then evaluate accumulating arithmetic sums and reciprocal sums while parsing: each column must receive additions in precisely its original row order, with unchanged division timing. Avoid approximate decimal conversion, restricted numeric ranges, or reassociated reductions. Buffer output only while retaining libc formatting, seven metric lines, one decimal place, and trailing spaces. Separate parsing gains from accumulation-fusion gains in the available measurements.",
      "C": "Research column-level execution and kernel fusion. Keep each column's complete statistical computation together, with original-order mean/harmonic reductions, sorting, then sorted-order variance. If the unchanged build already supports threading, evaluate one coarse-grained region using at most four column workers, private sorting scratch, and disjoint results; do not introduce compiler or build-setting changes. Compare serial, two-worker, and four-worker execution within the existing budget, retaining a dimension/work-based serial fallback because the baseline is short. Otherwise pursue the serial fused kernel and reduced allocation overhead. Do not parallelize within-column reductions, substitute the cancellation-prone sum-of-squares variance formula, or assume pow is an expensive call without evidence.",
      "G": "Integrate by measured selection, not presumed additive speedups. Establish the fastest correct standalone tree result, then evaluate compatible combinations within the existing budget, prioritizing A's algorithmic kernel with B's input path. Add C's scheduling only when supported and demonstrably beneficial; reassess its serial threshold after removing quadratic work. Reconcile ownership of input-time sums versus worker-time sums so they are neither duplicated nor reordered, and allocate scratch safely per active worker. Audit mode ties/narrowing, exceptional values, degenerate dimensions, median indexing, variance order, and exact output formatting. Use the unchanged oracle, compiler, target, validation, and timing procedure. Retain the best measured correct standalone program if integration regresses, and report correctness, timings, memory costs, and remaining semantic concerns.",
      "analysis": "The supplied implementation is Problem B, not the other problems in the document. It already stores columns contiguously. Both bubble sorting and pairwise mode counting cost O(columns * rows^2), making their joint replacement the strongest algorithmic objective. Arithmetic and harmonic sums occur before sorting, while variance is accumulated afterward; changing those orders can change one-decimal output. moda_aux reads uninitialized counters and narrows its answer through float, requiring explicit correctness attention rather than allocator-dependent optimization. This run provides only a valid four-case baseline averaging 10.463 ms, with no dimensions or profile. Consequently, I/O and threading overhead may matter, but neither is established as dominant. Research should remain portable to four ARM64 CPU cores, preserve every valid input, and judge gains through the fixed measurement procedure."
    },
